        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "894c3bc9-a279-558d-aa83-5bfc16ba222b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Colin Kolles, Romulus Kolles\n- Organizations: Hispania Racing F1 Team, Jordan, Midland F1, Spyker F1 Team, Force India, Jordan Grand Prix, ByKolles Racing\n- Events: 2007 Formula One World Championship\n- Topics: Formula One, team ownership and renaming, team management, motor racing foundations\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Kolles was born as Călin Colesnic on 13 December 1967 in Timişoara, Romania.\n- ByKolles Racing was founded in 2000 by Romulus Kolles and his son Colin Kolles as Kolles Racing.\n- Kolles Racing initially competed in German Formula 3 before moving to the F3 Euro Series from 2003 to 2005.\n- Colin Kolles held a senior team management role at the Formula One team known as Jordan, Midland, Spyker, and Force India from 2005 to 2008.\n- Spyker F1 Team was created by Spyker Cars after buying the short-lived Midland F1 team, which had formerly been Jordan Grand Prix.\n- Spyker F1 Team, sponsored as Etihad Aldar Spyker F1 Team, competed in the 2007 Formula One World Championship.\n- At the end of the 2007 season, Spyker F1 Team was sold and renamed Force India.\n- Colin Kolles later became the former team principal and managing director of the Hispania Racing F1 Team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9e66c62e-f771-546f-9e87-c033814998ea",
        "text": "Page: Colin Kolles. Sentence: Colin Kolles (born Călin Colesnic 13 December 1967 in Timişoara, Romania) is the former team principal and managing director of the Hispania Racing F1 Team, previously holding a similar position at the team known under the names Jordan, Midland, Spyker and Force India from 2005 to 2008.\nPage: Spyker F1. Sentence: The Spyker F1 Team, known as the Etihad Aldar Spyker F1 Team for sponsorship reasons was a Formula One team that competed in the 2007 Formula One World Championship, and was created by Spyker Cars after their buyout of the short-lived Midland F1 (formerly Jordan Grand Prix) team.\nPage: Spyker F1. Sentence: At the end of the 2007 season the team was sold and renamed Force India.\nPage: ByKolles Racing. Sentence: Founded in 2000 by Romulus Kolles and his son Colin Kolles as Kolles Racing, the company initially participated in German Formula 3 before moving to the F3 Euro Series from 2003 to 2005.",
